  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <table style="width: 100%;">
      <tr>
        <td style="width: 30%;">Company Name</td>
        <td style="width: 30%;">Mailing address</td>
        <td style="width: 20%;">State</td>
        <td style="width: 10%;">Zip code</td>
        <td style="width: 10%;">Country (if not U.S.A.)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><span data-field="employer.name">{{ employer.name }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="employer.address">{{ employer.address }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="employer.state">{{ employer.state }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="employer.zip_code">{{ employer.zip_code }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="employer.country">{{ employer.country }}</span></td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <table style="width: 100%;">
      <tr>
        <td style="width: 30%;">Employee's Social Security Number or TIN</td>
        <td style="width: 30%;">Employee's contact email address</td>
        <td style="width: 20%;">Employee's date of hire (MM/DD/YYYY)</td>
        <td style="width: 20%;"></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><span data-field="employee.ssn">{{ employee.ssn }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="employee.email">{{ employee.email }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="employee.hire_date">{{ employee.hire_date }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Question 9: Enter the wages earned by the employee during the last eight weeks preceding the PFL start date. The gross amount paid is the employee's gross weekly pay, including any overtime and tips earned for that week, plus the weekly prorated amount of any bonuses or commission received during the preceding 52 weeks. (For detailed steps, see chart on page 2 of the instructions.) Calculate the gross average weekly wage by adding up the gross amounts paid, and then divide by eight (or number of weeks worked if less than eight).</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <table style="width: 100%;">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th style="width: 10%;">Week no.</th>
          <th style="width: 30%;">Week ending date (MM/DD/YYYY)</th>
          <th style="width: 20%;">Number of days worked</th>
          <th style="width: 20%;">Gross amount paid</th>
          <th style="width: 20%;">Check Days Normally Worked</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for i in range(1, 9) %}
        <tr>
          <td>{{ loop.index }}</td>
          <td><span data-field="wage_data[{{ loop.index0 }}].week_ending_date">{{ wage_data[loop.index0].week_ending_date }}</span></td>
          <td><span data-field="wage_data[{{ loop.index0 }}].days_worked">{{ wage_data[loop.index0].days_worked }}</span></td>
          <td><span data-field="wage_data[{{ loop.index0 }}].gross_amount">{{ wage_data[loop.index0].gross_amount }}</span></td>
          <td>
            <label><input type="checkbox"> Monday</label>
            <label><input type="checkbox"> Tuesday</label>
            <label><input type="checkbox"> Wednesday</label>
            <label><input type="checkbox"> Thursday</label>
            <label><input type="checkbox"> Friday</label>
            <label><input type="checkbox"> Saturday</label>
            <label><input type="checkbox"> Sunday</label>
          </td>
        </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Calculated average gross weekly wage:</p>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">$\text{<span data-field="calculated_average_weekly_wage">{{ calculated_average_weekly_wage }}</span>}$</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">*As SUNY employees are paid bi-weekly, please note each pay period will be divided by two to get to a weekly gross paid amount (i.e. Pay period #1 an employee receives \$3,000 - week 1 and week 2 amounts will each be \$1,500).</p>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">10a. If employee received or will receive full wages while on PFL, will employer be requesting reimbursement? <span data-field="reimbursement_request">{{ reimbursement_request }}</span> Yes No</p>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">10b. Through what date will the employee receive full wages? (MM/DD/YYYY) <span data-field="full_wage_end_date">{{ full_wage_end_date }}</span></p>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">10c. Through what day will the employee's work obligations extend? <span data-field="work_obligation_end_date">{{ work_obligation_end_date }}</span></p>
  </div>
</div>

